{{/*
The commit identity `/git-identity:use private` points GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL at.

The [include] line comes first on purpose, and is the reason this file is a
template rather than a copy: GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL *replaces* the global config
rather than layering onto it, so without the include every other setting -
core.autocrlf, init.defaultBranch, aliases - silently disappears in any project
bound to this profile. Only the [user] block below is meant to win.

On `managed` this is the point of the whole plugin: personal work on the work Mac
commits as the personal address instead of the employer one. On `owned` the
machine default is already this address, so the file is a no-op - kept anyway, so
both Macs answer `/git-identity:use private` identically and the registry needs no
branch.
*/ -}}
[include]
	path = {{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/.gitconfig

[user]
	name = {{ .identity.name }}
	email = {{ .identity.personalEmail }}
